<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees Dec CPI at 2.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees Dec CPI at 2.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Italy 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its December consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Florence's inflation rate was 0.3 percent and 2.1 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Florence is one of 10 Italian cities which to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.08 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.3)     2.1  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0  (-0.1)     2.0  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.3   (0.1)     2.5  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0   (0.9)     5.2  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1   (0.7)     2.4  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.1)     2.1  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.1   (0.4)     0.9  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.2   (0.2)     0.5 (-0.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (1.5)     3.7  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     3.4  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2   (0.3)     1.3  (1.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
